posixos.c: the jobserver's state is a ledger, a struct the verbs take, and make's own is
the goals ledger behind the stock names; amk opens more by jobserver_new and the _on
verbs, declared in amk.h. The wait for a token also serves the children's call requests,
so a child blocked on a request never holds a token make is waiting for; it takes its
bound in milliseconds, forever below zero, and at once at zero. A ledger's token is width
bytes, one for make's own; a ledger whose tokens are labels sets its width by
jobserver_width_on, reads the token the last acquire took whole by jobserver_token_on, and
writes one by jobserver_release_token_on.

